      "side": 1,
      "message": "One thing: the check and the increment still aren\u0027t atomic, so each concurrent trimmer can overshoot by one. With tail\u003d1, trim\u003d3: A increments to 2 (deletes 1), B to 3 (deletes 2), A sees its stale 2 \u003c\u003d 3 and increments to 4 (deletes 3), B sees its stale 3 \u003c\u003d 3 and increments to 5 and deletes event 4. So it\u0027s bounded at k-1 extra events for k trimmers rather than prevented. Correct me if I am wrong?",
      "revId": "a3153c3f61202037a28b06c314bcb3332b070bf9",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
